e economy.\par \par \uc2 A modern-day gold rush is giving a big boost to U.S. GDP.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Chip Makers Are Profiting Off AI at the Expense of Just About Everyone Else\par \par \uc2 We are witnessing an extraordinary transfer of cash from the providers of AI-and, perhaps one day, AI users-to memory-chip makers.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Kevin Warsh\uc2  Invokes \uc2 Alan Greenspan\uc2  to Shrink the Fed-and Strengthen Its Chair\par \par \uc2 The approach of the new \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  head might not always align with the standard his predecessor set.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Week Ahead for FX, Bonds: U.S. Jobs Data in Focus as Markets Search for Clues on Fed Rate Path\par \par \uc2 U.S. jobs data could confirm indications that the economy is robust as investors gauge whether and when the Fed might raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Bond yields are falling as inflation pops. The Fed's tough talk under Warsh is helping.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Warsh\uc2 , the new Federal Reserve chair, is helping coax Treasury yields lower by talking tough on inflation.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Trump Threatens 100% Tariff on European Countries That Impose Digital Services Tax\par \par \uc2 The threat comes a day after the \uc2 European Union\uc2  approved tariff reductions on U.S. goods.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Consumer Sentiment Improves in June as Gasoline Prices Moderate\par \par \uc2 Consumer sentiment improved from recent record lows in June as gasoline prices moderated, according to the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 's monthly survey.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Fed's Kashkari Says the Fed May Have to Raise Rates This Year\par \par \uc2 Minneapolis Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Neel Kashkari\uc2  said inflation risks have led him to pencil in one rate hike by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Warsh Taps Two Veteran Fed Economists as Advisers\par \par \uc2 Daniel Covitz and Eric Engstrom, longtime Fed staffers, will assist the new chairman on policy and analysis.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 China Sharpens Tools for Hitting Back at Foreign Sanctions\par \par \uc2 Beijing is preparing a new law that would add to its ability to punish foreign companies and individuals deemed to harm Chinese interests.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 28, 2026 23:00 ET (03:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t00046\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
