\par\par \b \uc2 AI Hardware Boom to Continue to Power Asia PMIs -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 158 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 06:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0430 GMT - PMIs across much of Asia this week are expected to highlight the manufacturing boom amid demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  hardware, \uc2 Frederic Neumann\uc2 , chief Asia economist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , writes in a report. Export data from key electronics suppliers South Korea and Vietnam will likely show strength, helped by the boost in AI hardware supply chains in Asia, he writes. However, risks to inflation for most of Asia remain tilted to the upside due to the delayed effect of higher energy and commodity prices earlier this year, he says. In India, while the growth outlook has improved on lower oil prices, El Nino now threatens food prices and the informal sector, he says. Still, latest flash \uc2 PMI\uc2  data suggests that the Indian manufacturing sector should stay resilient, he adds. (kimberley.kao@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2026 00:30 ET (04:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t000bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
