\par\par \b \uc2 HK Bourse: Announcement From OP Financial On Change In Directors\b0\par\par\uc2 1,371 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 16:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For full details, please click on the following link: \par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0629/2026062902633.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0629/2026062902633.pdf}}}\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  and The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong \par Limited take no responsibility for the contents of this announcement, make no \par representation as to its accuracy or completeness and expressly disclaim any liability \par whatsoever for any loss howsoever arising from or in reliance upon the whole or any part \par of the contents of this announcement. \par  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 HK.AI CAPITAL LIMITED\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par (formerly known as WEALTHINK AI-INNOVATION CAPITAL LIMITED) \par (Incorporated in the Cayman Islands with limited liability) \par  \par (1) RESIGNATION OF NON-EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR \par  \par (2) APPOINTMENT OF NON-EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR \par  \par (3) CHANGE OF CHAIRMAN \par  \par (4) CHANGE IN COMPOSITION OF BOARD COMMITTEE AND \par  \par (5) CHANGE OF AUTHORISED REPRESENTATIVE \par RESIGNATION OF NON-EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR \par  \par     The board (the "Board") of directors ("Director") of \f28 \uc2 \f2 HK.AI Capital Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  (the \par "Company") announces that Dr. Wang Qin has tendered his resignation as a non-executive \par Director, and will cease to act as the chairman of the Board, the chairman of the nomination \par committee (the "Nomination Committee") of the Company, and one of the authorised \par representative (the "Authorised Representative") of the Company under Rule 3.05 of the \par Rules (the "Listing Rules") Governing the Listing of Securities on The Stock Exchange of \par Hong Kong Limited (the "Stock Exchange"), all with effect from June 30, 2026. Dr. Wang \par Qin has indicated that he wished to focus on his other career developments. \par  \par     Dr. Wang Qin has confirmed that he had no disagreement with the Board and that there is \par no matter relating to his resignation that needs to be brought to the attention of the \par shareholders of the Company and The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited. \par  \par     The Board would like to take this opportunity to express its gratitude to Dr. Wang Qin for \par his valuable contributions to the Board and the Company during his tenure of services. \par  \par     -1- \par APPOINTMENT OF NON-EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR \par  \par     The Board hereby announces that, Prof. Lin Jing will be appointed as a non-executive \par Director of the Company with effect from June 30, 2026. \par  \par     Prof. Lin Jing ("Prof. Lin"), aged 43, is an executive with nearly 20 years of global \par experience in enterprise \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ("AI") strategy and digital solutions. \par  \par     Prof. Lin graduated from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 University of Science and Technology of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  in July 2004, \par receiving Dual Bachelor's degrees in Finance from the Department of Statistics and \par Finance, and obtained a Master's degree in Engineering Mechanics from the same university \par in June 2009. Subsequently, she received her Ph.D. degree in Finance from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 City \par University of Hong Kong\f28 \uc2 \f2  in July 2013. \par  \par     Prof. Lin is currently the Chief Scientist of \f28 \uc2 \f2 GoFintech Quantum Innovation Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  (Stock \par Code: 290). She has been also serving as the Chief AI and Data Scientist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Hong \par Kong Jockey Club\f28 \uc2 \f2  since January 2022, where she collaborates with executive leadership to \par implement AI solutions aimed at enhancing operational efficiency, revenue growth, and \par market expansion. Prof. Lin has also served as the Co-founder of the Silicon Valley-China \par CIO Alliance since September 2015, establishing cross-border Go-to-Market strategies and \par collaborating with global technology leaders such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nvidia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alphabet\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 AWS\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Databricks\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Alibaba, Tencent and ByteDance to integrate innovative tools into enterprise \par workplaces. Prof. Lin has extensive industry experience. She served as the Head of Big \par Data at Ping An Property & Casualty Insurance from 2019 to 2021, and as the Director of \par Strategy and Operations for the cash loan business at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Baidu\f28 \uc2 \f2 's FinTech initiatives from 2017 \par to 2019. She held the positions of Chief Data Scientist at Aegon Asia from 2015 to 2017 \par and Senior Manager at Cigna Asia Pacific from 2012 to 2015. \par  \par     Prof. Lin is an advisor expert for the Shanghai Advanced Institute of Finance at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shanghai \par Jiao Tong University\f28 \uc2 \f2  and currently serves as a Professor of Practice at the Department of \par Computer Science of the City University of Hong Kong, a Researcher Fellow at the \par Shanghai Advanced Institute of Finance of Shanghai Jiao Tong University, and an industry \par tutor at the Business School of the University of Science and Technology of China. She \par also serves as a council member for the Hong Kong Society of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Artificial Intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \par Robotics (HKSAIR). Prof. Lin holds three United States patents in the field of data science \par related to predictive modeling and the next-best-offer optimization. \par  \par     Prof. Lin will hold the office of non-executive Director from June 30, 2026 until the first \par annual general meeting of the Company after her appointment, subject to retirement by \par rotation and re-election in accordance with the Listing Rules and the articles of association \par of the Company. Prof. Lin has entered into a service contract with the Company, pursuant \par to which Prof. Lin is entitled to a director's fee of HK$360,000 per annum. Prof. Lin's \par -2- \par remuneration was determined by the Board (the "Remuneration Committee") pursuant to \par the recommendation made by the remuneration committee of the Company with reference to \par her duties and responsibilities within the Company, the prevailing market conditions of \par companies of comparable size and similar operations, and will be subject to review by the \par Remuneration Committee from time to time. \par  \par     Save as disclosed above, Prof. Lin (i) does not have any relationship with any director, \par senior management, substantial or controlling shareholder (having the meaning ascribed to \par it in the Listing Rules) of the Company; (ii) does not hold any other positions in the \par Company or its subsidiaries; and (iii) did not hold any directorship in the past three years in \par other public companies, the securities of which are listed on any securities market in Hong \par Kong or overseas. As at the date of this announcement and within the meaning of Part XV \par of the Securities and Futures Ordinance, Prof. Lin does not have any interests in the shares \par of the Company. \par  \par     Other than as disclosed above, there are no other matter in relation to the appointment of \par Prof. Lin as a non-executive Director that needs to be brought to the attention of the \par shareholders of the Company, nor is there any information that should be disclosed pursuant \par to Rule 13.51(2) of the Listing Rules. \par  \par     The Board would like to extend its warmest welcome Prof. Lin in joining the Board. \par  \par     CHANGE OF CHAIRMAN \par Following the resignation of Dr. Wang Qin as a non-executive Director, he will cease to be \par the chairman of the Board with effect from June 30, 2026. \par  \par     The Board hereby announces that, Prof. Lin, a non-executive Director, has been elected as \par the chairlady of the Board with effect from June 30, 2026. \par  \par     CHANGE IN COMPOSITION OF BOARD COMMITTEE \par Following the resignation of Dr. Wang Qin as a non-executive Director, he will cease to be \par the chairman of the Nomination Committee with effect from June 30, 2026. With effect \par from June 30, 2026, Prof. Lin will be appointed as the chairlady of the Nomination \par Committee. \par  \par     Following the above change, the Nomination Committee includes one director of a different \par gender and continues to comprise a majority of independent non-executive Directors. The \par Nomination Committee consists of one non-executive Director (Prof. Lin) and three \par independent non-executive Directors (Mr. Yan Xiaotian, Mr. Zhao Kai and Mr. He \par Hongchun), with Prof. Lin acting as the chairlady. \par  \par     -3- \par The above change is made in compliance with code provision B.3.5 set out in the Corporate \par Governance Code as contained in Appendix C1 to the Listing Rules. The Board is of the \par view that the implementation of such change will enhance the effectiveness and diversity of \par the Nomination Committee and further promote the overall good corporate governance \par practices of the Company. \par  \par     CHANGE OF AUTHORISED REPRESENTATIVE \par Following the resignation of Dr. Wang Qin as a non-executive Director, he will cease to be \par the authorised representative of the Company with effect from June 30, 2026. With effect \par from June 30, 2026, Prof. Lin will be appointed as an authorised representative of the \par Company under Rule 3.05 of the Listing Rules. \par  \par Source: Hong Kong Exchanges & Clearing \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 29, 2026 10:52 ET (14:52 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t002da\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
