\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: AI Trading Bot Adoption Rises Across Global Markets as Retail Investors Embrace Automation\b0\par\par\uc2 942 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2026\par 08:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Growth in stock and cryptocurrency markets has coincided with increased adoption of AI trading tools. This report, prepared by the Monday Newswire LTD editorial team, examines independent market trends shaping the use of automated trading technologies in 2026.\par \par \uc2 London, United Kingdom, June 28, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- As global financial markets continue to undergo rapid digital transformation, demand for AI-powered trading tools is growing across both stock and cryptocurrency markets. Independent market analysis and industry reporting indicate that AI-driven trading systems and algorithmic tools are increasingly influencing retail investor behavior worldwide.\par \par \uc2 AI Trading Tools Emerge as Key Driver of Multi-Asset Market Growth\par \par \uc2 Industry analysts and fintech researchers report that retail investor adoption of AI trading tools is rising steadily, with measurable differences observed across asset classes. According to aggregated third-party market data compiled from multiple independent sources: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- AI trading tool adoption in cryptocurrency markets increased by over 40% \par       year-on-year \par  \par    -- Automated trading system usage in stock markets rose by approximately 28% \par  \par    -- Algorithmic trading penetration continues to expand in forex markets \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts note that this trend reflects a structural shift from discretionary trading toward data-driven, model-based decision-making among retail investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AI Trading Bots Are Reshaping Retail Investment Behavior\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to fintech industry experts, AI trading bots powered by machine learning models, real-time data analysis, and automated execution systems are being credited with improving trading efficiency while reducing emotional decision-making among retail participants.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industry research highlights several operational advantages that automated trading systems provide over manual approaches, including: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Real-time analysis of high-frequency market data \par  \par    -- Automated identification of trends and trading signals \par  \par    -- Millisecond-level trade execution capabilities \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industry experts believe this evolution is driving retail investors toward a new stage of strategy automation and accelerating the mainstream adoption of intelligent trading systems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fintech Platforms Simplify Onboarding to Accelerate AI Trading Adoption\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fintech companies operating in the AI trading space have focused on reducing barriers to entry for retail investors. A growing number of platforms have streamlined onboarding processes to enable faster access to automated trading tools without requiring advanced financial or technical expertise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Typical onboarding workflows for AI trading platforms generally involve three stages: account setup and verification, strategy configuration based on risk tolerance and capital allocation, and activation of automated trading with performance monitoring through visual dashboards.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One platform operating in this space is \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=yhmjAWl9rzNNbWArzTg8keYx9RB8aEn_71OG87lAm3bzQZ2YpfLn4fRazyzhSosTHe3G84lpbhs8qZ0LfUXiY5jwGejR8ITuSYFL5BS1vGw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=yhmjAWl9rzNNbWArzTg8keYx9RB8aEn_71OG87lAm3bzQZ2YpfLn4fRazyzhSosTHe3G84lpbhs8qZ0LfUXiY5jwGejR8ITuSYFL5BS1vGw}}}\uc2 \f2 = QuantRate, a fintech company focused on AI-driven quantitative trading infrastructure. The platform offers retail and institutional investors access to automated trading solutions, with tools for configuring AI trading strategies across multiple asset classes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market Data: Strong Growth in AI Trading Tool Demand\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Independent market research tracking search behavior and platform adoption trends points to significant growth in retail investor interest in automated trading solutions in 2026: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Global search volume for "AI trading tools" increased by more than 55% \par       year-on-year, according to third-party search analytics providers \par  \par    -- "Automated trading system for beginners" has become one of the \par       fastest-growing retail investment-related search queries \par  \par    -- Asia leads global growth in adoption, followed by Europe and North \par       America \par  \par    -- Demand for automated stop-loss and AI strategy tools is rising \par       significantly in crypto markets \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industry researchers note that this growth is being driven not only by professional traders but also by retail investors seeking automated and passive investment solutions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risk Management and Strategy Optimization Become Industry Priorities\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As AI trading tools gain broader adoption, risk management has emerged as a key focus area within the fintech sector. Next-generation AI trading systems are increasingly incorporating: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Dynamic risk assessment and position sizing mechanisms \par  \par    -- Volatility-based strategy adjustment protocols \par  \par    -- Multi-asset portfolio rebalancing models \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These capabilities aim to improve system stability and performance across varied market conditions, reducing exposure to extreme volatility events.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expanding the Intelligent Quantitative Trading Ecosystem\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beyond execution capabilities, industry participants are working to build open strategy ecosystems that allow developers and quantitative traders to upload, test, and share algorithmic trading models. This initiative is contributing to what analysts describe as an emerging "AI quantitative strategy marketplace," enabling broader distribution of trading strategies across different asset classes and risk profiles.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industry analysts believe that over the next three to five years, AI-powered automated trading platforms will become a significant growth segment within fintech, with infrastructure scalability and strategy ecosystems serving as key competitive differentiators.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 About QuantRate\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=yhmjAWl9rzNNbWArzTg8kaJK5lMZTPFoft6lZZniW_8cNDcHAfnkLxnMQFjhYyeXQhS-BbRiNcHF_Dfeoy1RFCDiK2Hlj4p4295UJ2n_lE4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=yhmjAWl9rzNNbWArzTg8kaJK5lMZTPFoft6lZZniW_8cNDcHAfnkLxnMQFjhYyeXQhS-BbRiNcHF_Dfeoy1RFCDiK2Hlj4p4295UJ2n_lE4}}}\uc2 \f2 = QuantRate is a fintech company focused on AI-driven financial technology and intelligent quantitative trading infrastructure. The company provides automated trading solutions for retail and institutional investors worldwide, combining \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  algorithms, real-time market data analysis, and global trading connectivity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Media Contact:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 QuantRate Press Office\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Email: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=us8sdaCgESk8sx5v5YnqpaPkC6UCrLwEk5pZWTwuIPxbMe4zdu5B-2w-vGBZbwDMuV2IKzhPkf6iQxrBXfkJ3hP95MazHn0jgGCLTHlyJqk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=us8sdaCgESk8sx5v5YnqpaPkC6UCrLwEk5pZWTwuIPxbMe4zdu5B-2w-vGBZbwDMuV2IKzhPkf6